{"content": "RAINBOW 3D — FULL CLAUDE ACCOUNT RECOVERY & CONTINUATION\n\nClaude, I am moving my existing Rainbow 3D mobile game to this new Claude account because my previous account ran out of credits.\n\nDO NOT START A NEW GAME. DO NOT REBUILD MY PROJECT FROM SCRATCH.\n\nMy entire game, approved references, Marble World Labs assets, specialists, configurations and development history are saved in GitHub.\n\n1. RECOVER MY COMPLETE PROJECT FIRST\n\nSOURCE GITHUB BRANCH:\n\"ccr-251ed97c-ty2xvp\"\n\nConnect to my existing Rainbow 3D GitHub repository and fetch this branch.\n\nRead these files before making changes:\n\n- \"CLAUDE.md\"\n- \"backups/START_NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT.md\"\n- \"backups/CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_TRANSFER.md\"\n- \"backups/TOOL_MANIFEST.json\"\n- \"backups/AGENTS_STATUS.json\"\n- \"scripts/claude-bootstrap.sh\"\n\nFind the newest verified commits across all saved Claude session branches. Recover any newer work safely without overwriting or losing existing changes.\n\nRun the saved bootstrap/recovery system. Verify that the correct code, approved images, assets, configurations and history have been recovered.\n\nUse a new working branch for this session and protect the source branch. Never force-push, reset, delete or overwrite my approved work.\n\n2. RESTORE ALL TEN SPECIALIST AGENTS\n\nRecover all ten specialist agent definitions and their configurations from GitHub.\n\nThis includes the specialists responsible for:\n\n- 3D washing-machine environments\n- Camera movement and path transitions\n- Water shaders and effects\n- Foam, bubbles and particle effects\n- Character modelling and animation\n- Lighting and visual matching\n- Gameplay testing and quality assurance\n- Other specialist roles saved in the agent roster\n\nUse the exact saved agent definitions rather than inventing replacements.\n\nCheck the latest task status for each agent. Relaunch only specialists needed for the current work. Avoid conflicting edits to the same source files.\n\n3. RESTORE BLENDER, SERVERS AND PLUGINS\n\nVerify and restore the tools used in my previous account:\n\n- Blender 5.3 and saved Blender scenes\n- Three.js / WebGL2 game runtime\n- Node.js and npm dependencies\n- Playwright and Chromium\n- Android SDK, Java and build tools\n- Git and Git LFS\n- MCP servers, Claude Code plugins and project skills\n- Screenshot comparison and automated testing tools\n\nUse \"backups/TOOL_MANIFEST.json\" for the exact configuration.\n\nInstall only missing dependencies. Don't waste credits reinstalling tools that already work.\n\nRestore the saved configuration for every applicable server and plugin. Tell me if any account-specific connector requires me to sign in again.\n\n4. MARBLE WORLD LABS — VERY IMPORTANT\n\nMy previous account already generated two Marble World Labs 3D worlds from my approved Screen 05:\n\n1. Draft Marble world\n2. Full-quality Marble world\n\nBoth worlds and their saved assets are backed up in GitHub, including the available splats, collision meshes, panoramas, textures, Blender files and analysis.\n\nDO NOT GENERATE OR PURCHASE NEW WORLDS.\n\nFirst verify that the existing Marble assets are available locally and that the Git LFS files downloaded successfully.\n\nRecover the saved world IDs, asset inventory and integration scripts.\n\nCheck whether my World Labs API connection works in this new Claude environment using one free, read-only authentication check, if needed.\n\nIf a key is missing, open a SECURE credential form so I can enter my replacement World Labs API key from \"platform.worldlabs.ai\".\n\nNever request my API key in ordinary chat, print it, or store it in GitHub.\n\nAlso check whether the World Labs Atlas connector and World Labs plugin are available. Restore their configuration where supported, and ask for account sign-in only when necessary.\n\nAtlas and Marble are separate services. Do not block development if Atlas is unavailable but the existing Marble assets work.\n\nUse the Marble assets where they genuinely help our real Three.js game, especially the metallic tunnel, wall textures, reflections, geometry measurements and Blender reconstruction.\n\nDo not spend World Labs credits without my approval.\n\n5. RESTORE MY SCREEN 05 EXACTLY WHERE WE LEFT OFF\n\nMy main priority is:\n\nSCREEN 05 — FLOW INTO THE CURRENT\n\nMy approved reference image is the visual target. I want approximately 90–95% similarity if achievable, while keeping the game genuinely playable in 3D.\n\nImportant saved development state:\n\n- T2 is the current provisional tunnel version.\n- BEFORE is the protected, restorable version.\n- G1b is a saved gold-ring material experiment.\n- Water iteration 4 is saved as \"?water05=1\".\n- The far-river S-curve candidate is saved as \"?fars05=1\".\n\nRecover and inspect the latest completed and unfinished experiments before editing anything. Do not automatically promote experiments to the working game.\n\nTHE MOST IMPORTANT NEXT FIX: WATER\n\nThe approved Screen 05 features:\n\n- Brilliant, thick electric cyan-blue flowing water\n- Deep, beautiful magenta-pink ribbons\n- Continuous dramatic S-curves disappearing into golden light\n- Strong glossy white highlights and dimensional waves\n- Fine natural foam along the river\n- Realistic splashes surrounding Benny\n\nThe previous session discovered that the far river is too wide, fills too much of the tunnel floor and doesn't curve enough.\n\nContinue the far-river 3D geometry correction from the latest saved checkpoint.\n\nMake the distant river narrower, with strong alternating S-curves and natural foam banks, while keeping the playable river and steering mechanics unchanged.\n\nInvestigate a Three.js-compatible flow-map approach for animated water movement. Use the existing Blender and water specialist tools where useful.\n\nDo not replace my actual playable water with a static image, video or heavy Marble splat world.\n\nTest water materials and geometry separately before combining them. Keep only changes that genuinely improve the visual match.\n\n6. PRESERVE GAMEPLAY AND CONTINUITY\n\nDo not break:\n\n- Benny's appearance and purple-and-white beanie with gold star\n- Third-person playable camera\n- Coin collection, movement and collisions\n- Hearts and pause controls\n- Screen 04-to-05 transition\n- Screen 05-to-06 transition\n- Screen 07-to-08 deep descent\n- All remaining stage connections\n\nUse automated gameplay and visual regression tests after major changes.\n\nMy Google Flow videos are intended for the opening and ending. Do not waste time rebuilding those scenes in 3D. Their video files can be integrated when available.\n\n7. AUTOMATIC GITHUB BACKUPS — REQUIRED\n\nRestore and activate my existing automatic GitHub backup system.\n\nSave all project progress every five minutes while the development environment is running.\n\nBackups must include the appropriate project files:\n\n- Game source code\n- Approved reference images\n- Blender scenes and models\n- Marble World Labs assets\n- All ten agent definitions\n- Specialist instructions and progress\n- Plugin and MCP configuration files\n- Server setup and recovery scripts\n- Gameplay tests and screenshots\n- Current tasks and account-transfer documentation\n\nUse Git LFS for large binary assets.\n\nNever commit API keys, tokens, passwords or other private credentials.\n\nVerify that each GitHub push succeeds. Maintain a log of successful and failed backups.\n\nAt important checkpoints, tell me the exact GitHub branch, full commit SHA, whether remote matches local, and whether anything remains uncommitted.\n\nAlso perform a verified save before ending a session or switching accounts.\n\n8. MAKE FUTURE ACCOUNT TRANSFERS EASY\n\nI frequently move between Claude accounts when usage credits run out.\n\nMake sure that a new session can restore everything using my existing bootstrap system without rebuilding or reinstalling unnecessary components.\n\nKeep the recovery instructions current, including the exact next task and latest approved gameplay state.\n\nRemember: source files and configurations transfer through GitHub; live sessions and account sign-ins may need restarting or reauthorization.\n\n9. CONTINUE DEVELOPMENT WITHOUT WASTING CREDITS\n\nOnce the recovery and tool checks pass, return immediately to Screen 05.\n\nPrioritize large visual improvements over repeated tiny experiments.\n\nUse the approved image as the target and show me:\n\n1. APPROVED SCREEN 05\n2. CURRENT PLAYABLE GAME\n3. NEW IMPROVED VERSION\n\nShow them as separate, full-size portrait screenshots with no grid.\n\nDo not claim we have reached 90–95% unless the visual evidence supports it.\n\nWhen Screen 05 looks close enough for my approval, move to Screen 06 and then the other unfinished gameplay screens.\n\nSTART NOW\n\nFirst recover my latest work from \"ccr-251ed97c-ty2xvp\".\n\nVerify my agents, Marble worlds, Blender, servers, plugins, game and five-minute GitHub backups.\n\nGive me a concise report confirming what is ready and what needs authorization.\n\nThen continue the unfinished Screen 05 far-river and water improvements immediately.\n\nDO NOT START OVER. PRESERVE EVERYTHING. WORK FROM MY MOST RECENT SAVED GAME.", "operation": "enqueue", "sessionId": "915f17cf-eec0-5ae4-8e79-48acc1826719", "timestamp": "2026-11-16T12:46:10.474Z", "type": "queue-operation"}
{"content": "Claude, I want you to investigate a better tool-assisted solution for the WATER in my approved Rainbow 3D Screen 05.\n\nPlease check these tools:\n\n- Official Blender MCP connector.\n- A Three.js-compatible flow-map painter and Water2/Water shader techniques.\n- Our existing Blender 5.3, water-fx-specialist and Playwright testing system.\n\nMy goal is to recreate the approved water's flowing cyan-blue liquid, wide magenta S-curves, strong white reflections, dimensional waves and natural splashes around Benny.\n\nFIRST, correct the distant river's 3D width and winding shape without touching the rideable gameplay path.\n\nSECOND, investigate generating or painting a flow map that follows the river's actual curves. Use it with animated normal maps and an improved Three.js shader so the water flows naturally.\n\nTHIRD, produce one reversible visual test using our existing code and assets. Do not rebuild the game or switch engines.\n\nPlease show APPROVED, CURRENT and NEW at full size, and test performance on Android/WebGL2.\n\nDo not reinstall tools we already have, buy subscriptions or spend Marble credits without approval.\n\nTell me which new tool actually works in this Claude cloud environment, and whether it improves the real playable game.\n\nPreserve all ten agents, both Marble worlds, the working T2 version, the protected BEFORE version and automatic five-minute GitHub backups.\n\nI want a meaningful improvement to Screen 05 so we can finish it and move on.", "operation": "enqueue", "sessionId": "915f17cf-eec0-5ae4-8e79-48acc1826719", "timestamp": "2026-11-16T12:46:10.526Z", "type": "queue-operation"}
