{"cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "claude/rainbow-3d-account-recovery-hfb8p0", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "1\t# water-fx-specialist, wave 10 (Screen 05 water) — test switch `?water05=1`\n2\t\n3\tGoal (user, 2026-11-16): the 05 water as close as possible to `references/05_flow_into_the_current.png` — thick\n4\tbrilliant cyan-blue liquid, rich flowing magenta-pink bands, continuous S-curves into the golden light, strong white\n5\tglossy highlights, layered movement, natural splashes around Benny; no flat stripes / runner track.\n6\tBaseline = CURRENT = `qa/pilot05/current_default_05.png` (default build, T2). Only Screen 05 water was touched; the\n7\triver width (course.ts), camera, gameplay, tunnel/rings/walls/lids, Benny and HUD are unchanged.\n8\t\n9\t## The switch\n10\t`WATER05` in `src/vfx/waterRibbon.ts` = `location.search` has `water05=1` (guarded: false in vite-node). Off, every\n11\tshader program and geometry attribute is the old one (`#ifdef WATER05` blocks, `+ coreShiftW10() = + 0`), so the\n12\tdefault build renders pixel-identically. Capture: `node scripts/capture.mjs 05 --out=DIR --q=water05=1`.\n13\t\n14\t## What I learned first (approved vs CURRENT, colour samples + masks, scratch tools)\n15\t* Approved cyan has R ≈ 0 (#00B5FB, #02C6FC, highlights aqua #21E0FC … #7DF9FA); CURRENT cyan is pastel\n16\t  (#46BDFF, #5FC7FF: R 0x30–0x60, B clipped) — the base palette was right, the white Fresnel / speculars / streak\n17\t  overlays pushed it pastel.\n18\t* Approved bands ramp in hue across each edge: hot pink #F92BD6 → violet #A14FE4 → periwinkle #866FF6 → blue\n19\t  #3FA3F9 → cyan over ≈40 px, and toward the bank to blue-violet #5F73F3 / deep #4287ED (the \"black\" gaps in the\n20\t  HSV masks). CURRENT cuts pink → cyan in 1–2 samples and its pink is lavender (#FF60FF).\n21\t* Approved near field = deep glossy blue with ∩-bowed bright crest arcs and ≈8–12 big jagged white flares;\n22\t  CURRENT = fanning rays, a grid of small stars, flat white lens pills. Approved splash = a wide fan of thin water\n23\t  threads; CURRENT = two dense white \"wings\".\n24\t* Far river (screen mapping from a scratch probe of the locked camera): the real ribbon's exit bend (s 174–181)\n25\t  jogged the visible core 478 → 547 px over only 18 rows (y 587 → 569) just before the far-block seam, then the\n26\t  far block swung back left — the \"blob\" at the VP. The far block drew a narrow body hugging the outer wall with\n27\t  thin bands on its banks, and a flat lavender foam sheet left of the seam (the \"wedge\", identified with a scratch\n28\t  debug-colour render). Note: the approved far river is WIDER than our whole floor chord at y 505–560 (e.g. y 525\n29\t  approved ≈ 355–630 incl. foam, our chord 415–583) — tunnel/camera geometry, not water.\n30\t\n31\t## Iterations (each: 05 capture with the switch, `tools/qa/diff05.py`, full-size visual comparison)\n32\tAll iterations: 86 draw calls / 567,415 triangles at the 05 checkpoint (identical to CURRENT; ≤130 / ≤650k);\n33\t0 console errors. Full table: `DIFF05_all_iterations.md`. Shares are crude HSV indicators, not a fidelity score.\n34\t\n35\t| band (y) | metric | APPROVED | CURRENT | it01 | it02 | it03 | it04 (NEW) |\n36\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n37\t| VP + far river 470–640 | cyan / pink / white % | 8.5 / 19.1 / 5.3 | 7.4 / 43.5 / 6.7 | 7.0 / 43.0 / 6.8 | 7.5 / 42.5 / 6.3 | 7.5 / 42.5 / 6.6 | 7.3 / 42.6 / 6.9 |\n38\t| mid river 640–1000 | cyan / pink / white % | 23.3 / 20.4 / 9.3 | 38.7 / 25.2 / 8.1 | 30.5 / 22.6 / 8.2 | 30.5 / 22.6 / 8.2 | 30.5 / 22.6 / 8.2 | 29.0 / 22.3 / 8.8 |\n39\t| Benny + near 1000–1536 | cyan / pink / white % | 32.1 / 12.7 / 8.1 | 49.1 / 15.6 / 10.3 | 49.4 / 15.0 / 9.7 | 49.2 / 15.0 / 9.7 | 48.8 / 15.1 / 9.3 | 47.5 / 15.0 / 9.7 |\n40\t| mid / near | mean saturation | 0.68 / 0.72 | 0.66 / 0.69 | 0.62 / 0.69 | 0.62 / 0.69 | 0.62 / 0.69 | 0.60 / 0.67 |\n41\t| S-swing px VP / mid / ne